<GuideLayout 
  title="The Squat-Proof Test: Ensuring Opacity in Performance Leggings" 
  type="QUALITY CONTROL"
  description="Nothing kills a brand faster than transparent leggings. Learn the science of fabric density (GSM) and interlock knitting."
>
  <h2>The Ultimate Confidence Test</h2>
  <p>For yoga and gym leggings, being "squat-proof" is non-negotiable. Transparency issues often lead to high return rates and negative reviews.</p>
  
  <h3>GSM: Grams per Square Meter</h3>
  <p>The density of the fabric is the primary factor. For high-performance leggings, we recommend a GSM of 250 to 320. Anything lower risk being "see-through" when stretched.</p>

  <h3>Interlock vs. Single Jersey</h3>
  <p>Interlock knitting creates a double-sided fabric that is naturally more opaque and durable than single jersey. It's the industry standard for premium squat-proof leggings.</p>

  <h3>In-Factory Testing</h3>
  <p>At Fitclo, we perform stretch-to-limit tests under bright studio lighting for every batch of leggings to ensure your customers feel confident in every move.</p>
</GuideLayout>
